  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Galactic Camp is an annual furry convention in Alameda, California, held aboard the USS Hornet, a World War II Essex-class aircraft carrier that is now the USS Hornet Sea, Air & Space Museum. It is run by the Galactic Camp Corporation, a 501(c)(3) non-profit, and unlike most furry conventions it has no guests of honor or themes. The first event, called Space Camp Party, was held March 10, 2018, at the Faction Brewing brewery as part of Nacho Husky's 30th birthday, and it drew 535 people. It was renamed Galactic Camp in 2019 because of a pre-existing trademark, and has been aboard the Hornet since. Its charity is the Aircraft Carrier Hornet Foundation.",
